<title>PORTUGAL: Share trade in Portugal's Reditus halted.</title>
<headline>Share trade in Portugal's Reditus halted.</headline>
<dateline>LISBON 1997-02-27</dateline>
<text>
<p>Portugal's Financial Markets Committee (CMVM) suspended trade in telecommunications and computer group Reditus on Thursday, a spokesman for the Lisbon bourse said.</p>
<p>Dealers said the suspension could be linked to a report in the Diario Economico financial daily that an offshore investment company, Greenville Securities, was seeking to take a 25 percent stake.</p>
<p>Company officials could not immediately be contacted for comment.</p>
<p>--Lisbon bureau 3511-3150035</p>
